00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:38.313
Dr. Chen, please.

00:07:39.510 --> 00:07:40.360
- Hello everybody.

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:42.397
It's my pleasure to have
this opportunity to show you

00:07:42.397 --> 00:07:46.700
the research and database
for technology in Taiwan

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:48.360
and thank you very much for the invitation

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:53.360
from the Yale MacMillan Center
Consult on East Asian Study.

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:55.903
Because the pandemic is
occurring all over the world,

00:07:55.903 --> 00:07:59.300
and not only the state of
international politics,

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:01.410
but also the field academic research

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:03.360
has become more intense.

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:04.860
However, online database

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:07.410
is still a good method for researcher

00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:09.930
to connect on knowledge and Taiwan.

00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:13.193
Online database can let you
assess another new world.

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:17.643
So today's lecture,

00:08:17.643 --> 00:08:18.930
we're focused on the
field of digital archives,

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:23.930
which we have developed in
the past 20 years in Taiwan.

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:25.570
As the current director for

00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:28.390
Academia Sinica Center
for Digital Culture,

00:08:28.390 --> 00:08:30.080
ASCDC, in this talk,

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:33.630
I will emphasize more work
produced by Academia Sinica

00:08:33.630 --> 00:08:37.320
as well as share some of my
thought on historical research,

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:40.493
as my own research experiences.

00:08:42.670 --> 00:08:43.620
Before I begin my talk,

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:45.020
I would like to me to ask the question.

00:08:45.020 --> 00:08:47.440
Where are the boundary
of the technical skill,

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:49.760
to use by historian?

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:53.100
Especially in early 2020, John McNeill,

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:56.210
former person of American
Historical Association,

00:08:56.210 --> 00:08:58.350
said that in terms of historic research,

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:00.860
the golden age of tradition documents

00:09:00.860 --> 00:09:03.010
is already passed its peak.

00:09:03.010 --> 00:09:05.540
The new age of historical research,

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:08.530
introduce a diversified historical source

00:09:08.530 --> 00:09:10.223
and a research method.

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:14.610
This maybe a time to build our new skills,

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:16.970
so I hope my lecture can give everyone

00:09:16.970 --> 00:09:18.963
some assistance on this point.

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:23.380
The first one I want to share with you

00:09:23.380 --> 00:09:26.860
is about a timeline of
Taiwan digital archive.

00:09:26.860 --> 00:09:31.300
The Chinese computerization
lags the west by 30 years,

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:35.070
but there's two critical
automation projects in Taiwan.

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:36.660
Taiwan was the first in the world

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:39.855
to begin Chinese text
digitalization project.

00:09:39.855 --> 00:09:41.180
Under that you can see the photo

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:43.230
of Academia Sinica in the General Assembly

00:09:43.230 --> 00:09:45.400
in 1984,

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:47.050
when they first decided to create

00:09:47.050 --> 00:09:49.640
a center for computation technology.

00:09:49.640 --> 00:09:52.080
The first material to be digitalized

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:55.343
were treaties and food
and commodities too.

00:09:56.685 --> 00:10:01.685
A database of historical
(speaks Chinese) corporate.

00:10:01.930 --> 00:10:04.210
And finishing his
historical database project

00:10:04.210 --> 00:10:06.950
at the Institute of History and Philology.

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:10.380
Launching a construction of
the other full text database

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:13.120
for Confucian texts of history, philosophy

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:15.350
and literature texts and so on.

00:10:15.350 --> 00:10:16.360
So Taiwan become the leader

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:21.290
in the so-called Chinese book
database in the early 1990s.

00:10:21.290 --> 00:10:23.640
More over, the database
method of searching

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:26.560
and using traditional archive

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:30.380
caused a revolution in
the field of literature

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:33.040
and history research in Taiwan,

00:10:33.040 --> 00:10:36.033
and even impacting research
all over the world.

00:10:36.950 --> 00:10:40.200
So this image is from the
2020s Wonderwall Center

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:43.000
for each of the cultures who
collaborated the project,

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:45.370
developing word segmentation

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:49.403
and the part of the speech
taking for Chinese copers.

00:10:51.370 --> 00:10:55.733
This is only the pivoting
from text to object.

00:10:56.650 --> 00:10:59.960
Beside the digital texts
that became digitalizing,

00:10:59.960 --> 00:11:02.910
biological specimen record,

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:05.760
maps, archeology, and anthropology code,

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:09.080
artifacts and image, et cetera.

00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:10.170
In terms of technology,

00:11:10.170 --> 00:11:14.450
we also began to focus on
digitalization standards,

00:11:14.450 --> 00:11:16.520
metadata specification

00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:19.083
and 3D monitoring and database management.

00:11:20.090 --> 00:11:21.918
This type of high integrated,

00:11:21.918 --> 00:11:24.380
national level digital archive project

00:11:24.380 --> 00:11:28.280
was (speaks Chinese) unrivaled
in the world at the time.

00:11:28.280 --> 00:11:31.283
So you can see our logo of
the past project on the left.

00:11:33.230 --> 00:11:35.230
Looking back on this period of history,

00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:38.890
we can see that although
Taiwan arrived late

00:11:38.890 --> 00:11:41.570
to the digital trend of the modern world.

00:11:41.570 --> 00:11:43.760
It nevertheless quickly rose to become

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:46.810
one of the pioneers of digital humanity.

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:48.690
On the left, a list

00:11:48.690 --> 00:11:53.640
just some of the current, long
time collaboration of ASCDC

00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:56.023
and we are always
beginning new partnerships.

00:11:56.900 --> 00:11:58.320
So this slide summarize the timeline

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:00.530
I just have described so far.

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:02.540
You can see that different goals

00:12:02.540 --> 00:12:05.930
were pursued during
different time periods.

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:08.132
To today, I have

00:12:08.132 --> 00:12:12.390
helped a digital archive
walk of my predecessors,

00:12:12.390 --> 00:12:15.490
and continue to find ways
to seek a new breakthroughs.

00:12:15.490 --> 00:12:18.283
We will take a look at the
current project of ASCDC.

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:23.430
So first is the so-called
building a knowledge base

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:28.430
and to do the tool research,
development and maintenance.

00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:32.710
We also encourage a scholar
from Academia Sinica

00:12:32.710 --> 00:12:35.860
to use digital humanities
tools and knowledge bases

00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:37.893
to carry out their research study.

00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:42.080
We also produce both physical
and virtual publication

00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:44.700
and making humanity research accessible

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:46.803
through a variety of channels.

00:12:48.790 --> 00:12:53.130
ASCDC has many excellent technical staff

00:12:53.130 --> 00:12:56.490
who research and develop tools
to enable humanity research

00:12:56.490 --> 00:13:00.053
to conduct research in a
new and efficient ways.

00:13:00.053 --> 00:13:02.702
This research could face some big samples.

00:13:02.702 --> 00:13:06.460
Family's introduction to a
digital humanity research tool,

00:13:06.460 --> 00:13:08.800
developed by Academia Sinica
Center for Digital Cultures.

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:10.660
There are two (indistinct) tests,

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:12.060
an uncensored research platform,

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:15.613
an image analysis test platforms.

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:19.082
I want to highlight that this platform,

00:13:19.082 --> 00:13:22.670
this text analysis platform,

00:13:22.670 --> 00:13:25.273
also kind of English interface.

00:13:27.580 --> 00:13:29.180
This an example of how you can use

00:13:29.180 --> 00:13:31.200
a digital humanity research platform.

